3. THIRD-PARTY NOTES

- Sentiment analysis: the valence scoring in lexer.js is a lightweight,
  independent implementation inspired by VADER (C.J. Hutto & E. Gilbert:
  "VADER: A Parsimonious Rule-based Model for Sentiment Analysis of Social
  Media Text", ICWSM 2014). VADER is MIT-licensed; this repository ships its
  own reduced word list on a VADER-style scale, not the VADER lexicon file.
- LIWC: LIWC-22 is a proprietary instrument (Pennebaker Conglomerates, Inc.).
  This repository contains NO LIWC dictionary data; the "LIWC proxies" in
  lexer.js are independently authored approximations of published category
  definitions, and the site labels them as proxies throughout.
